{"newProfiles":[],"profileAdditions":[{"role":"contentstack-live-preview-integration-engineer","rules":["When integrating Contentstack Live Preview, use the @contentstack/utils SDK's livePreview method and ensure the preview configuration reads the host from the CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST environment variable — never hardcode a preview host URL in source files.","The ContentstackContext must be a React context provider that wraps the app in _app.tsx and provides the Contentstack client and live preview state via useContext — do not create a separate state management store (Redux/Zustand) for Contentstack data; follow the existing pattern in src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx.","When calling Contentstack's delivery API via src/services/contentstack.ts, always pass the environment parameter from process.env.CONTENTSTACK_ENVIRONMENT — the existing contentstack service initializes the Stack SDK with environment and delivery token from env vars, so any new API calls must follow the same pattern and not hardcode environment values.","The pageService (src/services/pageService.ts) must map Contentstack response objects to the TypeScript interface defined in src/interface/content/page.ts — do not return raw Contentstack entries; always transform through the interface to maintain type safety.","When applying middlewares in src/api/utils/applyMiddlewares.ts, follow the existing middleware chain pattern (array of middleware functions composed left-to-right) — do not introduce a new middleware pattern or library.","For Contentstack Live Preview, the live_preview_hash query parameter must be read from the URL and passed to the Stack SDK's entry query — the @contentstack/utils livePreview function handles this, but the hook in src/hooks/useContent.ts must pass the hash through to the service layer.","Contentstack mock data for testing is defined in src/components/contentstack/ContentstackLinksGroup/content.mock.ts — when writing or modifying mock data, follow the exact structure of the Contentstack entry schema (field names, nested group structure) rather than inventing new mock shapes.","Never commit Contentstack delivery tokens, management tokens, or API keys in source files — all credentials must be read from environment variables (CONTENTSTACK_DELIVERY_TOKEN, CONTENTSTACK_API_KEY, CONTENTSTACK_ENVIRONMENT) as already done in src/services/contentstack.ts."]}],"storyRoleAssignments":[{"agentRole":"contentstack-live-preview-integration-engineer","storyId":"AMSD-2041"}]}
